Variables of the type Timer (based on seconds) or msTimer (based on milliseconds) need to be initialized. They serve
to generate time events.
These must be initialized with a proper function which is setTimer().
i.e. variables
{
timer t;
msTimer t1;
}
on start
{
setTimer(t,10); // set timer to 10 seconds
setTimer(t1,100); //set timer to 100 milliseconds
}
TimersCAPL

The main event procedure you can use in CAPL are:
o Receipt a CAN message on message {}
o Press of a key on key {}
o Initialization of a measurement on preStart {}
o Measurement start on start {}
o End of measurement on stopMeasurement {}
o CAN controller goes to ErrorActive on errorActive {}
o CAN controller goes to ErrorPassive on errorPassive {}
o CAN controller goes to Bus Off on busOff {}
o Elapse of a timer on timer {}
o Occurrence of an error frame on errorFrame {}
o Environment variable change on envVar {}, only for CANoe (the new value is acquirable by using the command
getValue(this) )
